WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.136
The foundation work begins with something homeowners cannot see.

2
00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:06.799
Wallace Shift built Datum to make that first conversation clearer.

3
00:00:07.430 --> 00:00:11.095
An interactive cutaway shows the house and soil across the seasons.

4
00:00:11.722 --> 00:00:17.047
A sample inspection report helps visitors understand what the service could deliver before they inquire.

5
00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:20.206
The crack decoder starts with the visitor’s concern.

6
00:00:20.466 --> 00:00:23.089
Choose where the crack appears and what it looks like.

7
00:00:23.722 --> 00:00:27.108
Answer a follow-up question and the displayed guidance changes.

8
00:00:27.368 --> 00:00:30.105
It is a guide, never a diagnosis.

9
00:00:30.722 --> 00:00:35.676
That concern carries into the inspection request, so the visitor does not have to explain it again.

10
00:00:36.305 --> 00:00:43.733
The form offers space for photos, property details, contact information, and a convenient visit window.

11
00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:48.533
The finished preview keeps the concern attached.

12
00:00:48.793 --> 00:00:51.214
This fictional demonstration sends nothing.

13
00:00:51.474 --> 00:00:55.023
It connects useful education with a more informed inquiry.
